WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.280
This is Sheprd: your terminals and your coding agents, together in one window.

2
00:00:07.282 --> 00:00:13.882
On the left are your spaces, one per project, and below them every agent at work.

3
00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:17.209
Click new to start a fresh space.

4
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:24.210
For a repository, a new worktree gives an agent its own branch and folder to work in.

5
00:00:27.305 --> 00:00:35.505
The agent button, next to the new tab button, opens a chat with Claude, Codex, Gemini or another agent.

6
00:00:35.513 --> 00:00:42.113
Ask for a change, and follow every file it reads, every edit and every test.

7
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:50.640
A chat is a native view of an agent running in a terminal. This button shows that terminal, and Chat brings the chat back.

8
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:56.690
Each space holds tabs, and each tab can split into panes, side by side.

9
00:00:56.778 --> 00:01:04.498
The activity bar opens more: an overview of your agents, pull requests, issues, usage and more.

10
00:01:11.741 --> 00:01:17.461
The status bar keeps an eye on the machine, and shows your plan usage when you turn it on.

11
00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:25.829
Devices lists every machine you work on. Add SSH hosts or cloud machines, and their agents show up here too.

12
00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:33.079
Agents can open web pages beside you too. Ask for a preview, and the page opens in a tab.

13
00:01:33.244 --> 00:01:39.924
Annotate it: click anything on the page, write what should change, and send it to the agent.

14
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:49.070
The agent gets your note, makes the change, and the page reloads.

15
00:01:49.399 --> 00:01:54.799
Settings opens on themes: hover one to try it on the whole window.

16
00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:05.890
Pick the sidebar layout, the status indicators, and how tabs look.

17
00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:18.470
That's the tour. Every feature has its own short guide below.
